# ActiveSupport core extensions the actions layer calls on *known* stdlib types.
# RBS core doesn't know them, and a known receiver + unknown method is a
# hard `Ruby::NoMethod` error (unlike unknown constants, which degrade to
# warnings) — so each one used in app/actions must be declared here.
# Grow deliberately, method by method, as annotation coverage expands; replace
# with the gem_rbs_collection activesupport signatures if/when they catch up
# with Rails 8.1 (documented follow-up in doc/project/type-checking.md).
class Time
  # Really ActiveSupport::TimeWithZone (Time.zone is always set — Rails defaults
  # to UTC), which is NOT an RBS subtype of Time (it only fakes is_a?(Time) at
  # runtime). Deliberately `untyped` rather than a false `Time` contract; add a
  # TimeWithZone class stub if a call site ever needs to chain off the result.
  def self.current: () -> untyped
end
